{#- Reusable markup, so pages stay readable.

    M1 · lattice — DESIGN.md §6. Cell 8, pitch 18; the ratio does not change at any
    scale, and opacity comes from --lat-op / --lat-op-inv only. Each instance needs its
    OWN <pattern id>, which is why this takes one: a single shared pattern defined in
    <head> would break the .inv colour swap, because currentColor inside a <pattern>
    resolves where the pattern is DEFINED, not where it is used.

    The parent needs .has-lat (position:relative; overflow:hidden) and the content above
    it needs position:relative — .wrap already does. -#}
{% macro lattice(id, inv=false) %}
  <svg class="lat{% if inv %} inv{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true">
    <defs><pattern id="lat-{{ id }}" width="18" height="18" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
      <rect width="8" height="8" fill="currentColor"/></pattern></defs>
    <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#lat-{{ id }})"/>
  </svg>
{% endmacro %}


{#- The objective function. DESIGN.md §8 "Math notation": displayed math is NOTATION,
    not a figure, so the block carries data-claim="none" — never data-claim-scan="off",
    which is reserved for legal copy. The surrounding prose is NOT exempt.

    Rendered as MathML rather than an image so it inherits currentColor, holds in all
    three theme states, and stays selectable.

    One constraint, no closed form — COPY.md records why both cuts were made. -#}
{% macro objective() %}
  <div class="math" data-claim="none">
    <math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
      <munder>
        <mo movablelimits="false">argmin</mo>
        <mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#x2026;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow>
      </munder>
      <munder><mo>&#x2211;</mo><mi>h</mi></munder>
      <mfrac>
        <mrow><msubsup><mi>W</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>&#x3C3;</mi><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow>
        <msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub>
      </mfrac>
      <mspace width="1.6em"/><mtext>subject to</mtext><mspace width="0.6em"/>
      <munder><mo>&#x2211;</mo><mi>h</mi></munder>
      <msub><mi>p</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>h</mi></msub>
      <mo>&#x2264;</mo><mi>B</mi>
    </math>
  </div>
{% endmacro %}


{#- M4 · tick rule. A hairline carrying graduated ticks, major reaching higher than
    minor. DESIGN.md §6: the cheapest way to make an empty margin read as an instrument
    face rather than as whitespace.

    NO viewBox, deliberately. With one, the ticks scale with the cell and compress into a
    smeared 3px-pitch smudge at wide widths. Without one, user units are CSS pixels and
    the pattern tiles at true size at every width. Adding a viewBox to "fix" it is the bug
    returning. -#}
{% macro tickrule(id) %}
  <div class="edge" aria-hidden="true">
    <svg width="100%" height="26" focusable="false">
      <defs>
        <pattern id="tick-{{ id }}" width="45" height="26" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <rect x="0"  y="12" width="1" height="14" fill="currentColor"/>
          <rect x="9"  y="19" width="1" height="7"  fill="currentColor"/>
          <rect x="18" y="19" width="1" height="7"  fill="currentColor"/>
          <rect x="27" y="19" width="1" height="7"  fill="currentColor"/>
          <rect x="36" y="19" width="1" height="7"  fill="currentColor"/>
        </pattern>
      </defs>
      <rect width="100%" height="100%" fill="url(#tick-{{ id }})"/>
      <rect x="0" y="25" width="100%" height="1" fill="currentColor"/>
    </svg>
  </div>
{% endmacro %}
